TRAIN: paired-error inference and local plasticity; reward network taught with clamped labels.
llvmpipe (LLVM 20.1.2, 256 bits) / predictive coding (software Vulkan on CPU); 7,200 normal neurons plus paired error populations, 4,214,784 shared w/-w connections. Eight nonnegative motor outputs.
Vulkan selected a CPU renderer. Hardware acceleration requires an accessible GPU and its Vulkan driver; use --list-devices and --device INDEX to select a different device.
Integration: 8 steps/frame, activity h=0.04, weight h=0.02, eta=1E-05, reward eta=1E-05. One local weight update/frame.
Main eta = base eta * (1 + total pleasure - total pain). Totals use normalized applied signals plus primitive sensations from the preceding feedback (ideal in train, inferred in play). Propagation gain stays 1.
Exploration pleasure is disabled. Inactivity pain ramps to 1 over five simulated seconds; meaningful displacement resets its raw target.
Nonprimitive pleasure/pain and primitive pleasure fade with a 60-update half-life. Primitive pain is unchanged.
Drive inputs = total pleasure + total pain * held U(0,1); noise refreshes every 12 frames. Negative reward factors reverse local plasticity.
Total error = SUM(E^2), statistics only. No actor/value objective, replay, backpropagation, biases or least-squares reward shortcut.
Level 1; maze geometry stage 1/5; corridor width 3; health drain, primitive pain and ideal training rewards retained. Checkpoint /tmp/pc-fps-unused.
